#. type: Title =
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zirek"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:4
msgid ""
"Software that reads and speaks the languages large vendors don't get around "
"to."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:7
msgid ""
"Two strands, and they meet: screen-reader support for under-served "
"languages, and the local neural speech synthesis that makes a screen reader "
"usable in the first place."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Screen readers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:15
msgid ""
"*https://github.com/ZirekHQ/dengjen-nvda[dengjen-nvda]* — NVDA add-on for "
"fast, fully local neural text-to-speech using Piper voices. No cloud "
"service, no account. Speech runs locally once voices are installed; "
"downloading and previewing voices requires an internet connection.  "
"Originated as a maintenance fork of mush42/sonata-nvda (renamed from Sonata "
"Neural Voices in v4.0.0)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:18
msgid ""
"*https://github.com/ZirekHQ/nvdaku[nvdaku]* — Kurdish (Kurmanji) "
"localisation for NVDA: interface translation, character descriptions, and a "
"symbol dictionary. Dates from 2018 and is *partial* — see Help wanted below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:21
msgid ""
"*https://github.com/ZirekHQ/nvda-addon-testkit[nvda-addon-testkit]* — "
"end-to-end testing for NVDA add-ons, against a real NVDA, in CI. Built to "
"keep the add-ons above honest across NVDA releases."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "Speech synthesis"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:26
msgid ""
"The stack underneath the add-on, originally built on "
"https://github.com/mush42[Musharraf Omer]'s work:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:29
msgid ""
"*https://github.com/ZirekHQ/dengjen-tts[dengjen-tts]* — cross-platform Rust "
"engine for neural TTS models (Piper, Kokoro, MeloTTS)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:31
msgid ""
"*https://github.com/ZirekHQ/dengjen-piper-rs[dengjen-piper-rs]* — Rust "
"bindings for running Piper TTS models directly, independent of the full "
"dengjen engine."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:34
msgid ""
"*https://github.com/ZirekHQ/dengjen-tashkeel[dengjen-tashkeel]* — diacritic "
"(tashkeel)  restoration for Arabic. Arabic is normally written without the "
"short vowels a synthesizer needs, so they have to be inferred before "
"anything can be spoken."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:38
msgid ""
"Kurmanji phoneme support is contributed upstream to "
"https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng[espeak-ng] rather than kept here, so "
"it reaches every project that uses it."
msgstr ""

