#. type: Title =
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/architecture.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Architecture"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/architecture.adoc:10
msgid ""
"This page shows how the ZirekHQ speech components relate to each other, as a "
"https://c4model.com/[C4] System Context diagram. Each component's own docs "
"break its internals down further (Container, Component, and a Code-level "
"diagram) — see xref:dengjen-tts:architecture.adoc[dengjen-tts], "
"xref:dengjen-nvda:architecture.adoc[dengjen-nvda], "
"xref:piper-rs:architecture.adoc[dengjen-piper-rs], and "
"xref:dengjen-tashkeel:architecture.adoc[dengjen-tashkeel]."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/architecture.adoc:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"C4Context\n"
"    Person(user, \"Screen reader user\")\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/architecture.adoc:22
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    System_Boundary(zirekhq, \"ZirekHQ\") {\n"
"        System(nvda_addon, \"dengjen-nvda\", \"NVDA add-on (Python). Loaded "
"in-process by NVDA as a synth driver.\")\n"
"        System(tts, \"dengjen-tts\", \"Rust neural TTS inference "
"engine. Exposes CLI, C ABI, Python, and gRPC frontends.\")\n"
"        System(tashkeel, \"dengjen-tashkeel\", \"Arabic diacritization "
"(tashkeel/harakat). Rust core with C ABI, Python, and Java bindings.\")\n"
"        System(piper_rs, \"dengjen-piper-rs\", \"Standalone Piper-format TTS "
"inference crate. Not currently consumed by any other ZirekHQ component.\")\n"
"    }\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/architecture.adoc:25
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    System_Ext(nvda, \"NVDA\", \"Open-source Windows screen reader\")\n"
"    System_Ext(voices, \"Voice model catalogue\", \"Piper / Kokoro / MeloTTS "
"ONNX voices, e.g. huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices\")\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/architecture.adoc:33
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    Rel(user, nvda, \"Uses\")\n"
"    Rel(nvda, nvda_addon, \"Loads as a synthesizer driver\")\n"
"    Rel(nvda_addon, tts, \"Synthesizes speech via gRPC, talking to a "
"vendored dengjen-tts-grpc binary\")\n"
"    Rel(tts, tashkeel, \"Optionally phonemizes Arabic input text "
"(feature-gated, opt-in)\")\n"
"    Rel(nvda_addon, voices, \"Downloads voices\")\n"
"    Rel(tts, voices, \"Loads ONNX voice models\")\n"
"    Rel(piper_rs, voices, \"Loads Piper ONNX voices\")\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/architecture.adoc:36
msgid "Two things worth calling out that aren't obvious from the individual repos:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/architecture.adoc:41
msgid ""
"*dengjen-nvda never talks to dengjen-tts as a library.* It launches a "
"separately vendored `dengjen-tts-grpc` binary as its own OS process and "
"speaks to it over gRPC — the two are only coupled at the process boundary, "
"not the API boundary."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/architecture.adoc:45
msgid ""
"*dengjen-piper-rs and dengjen-tashkeel are not wired into dengjen-tts's "
"default build.* dengjen-tashkeel is an optional, feature-gated dependency of "
"one of dengjen-tts's model crates; dengjen-piper-rs is a fully separate, "
"parallel implementation with no dependency relationship to dengjen-tts in "
"either direction."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/translating.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Translating the docs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/translating.adoc:8
msgid ""
"The site is built once per language by Antora, using AsciiDoc generated by "
"https://po4a.org/[po4a] from the same English source files every component "
"already publishes. A translated page always exists at the same path as its "
"English counterpart -- untranslated strings just render in English until "
"someone fills them in."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/translating.adoc:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "Filling in Kurmanji (kmr)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/translating.adoc:15
msgid ""
"Kurmanji translations live in a single catalog, `locale/kmr/docs.po`, at the "
"root of this repo. Open it in any PO editor (Poedit, Lokalize, a plain text "
"editor) and fill in the `msgstr` under any `msgid` you can "
"translate. Nothing else needs to change -- the next site build picks up your "
"edits."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/translating.adoc:24
msgid ""
"`make build` and CI always run po4a with `--no-update`, so routine builds "
"never rewrite the catalog files themselves -- they only ever read existing "
"`msgid`/`msgstr` pairs and fall back to English for anything not yet in the "
"catalog. If you add a new page or edit existing English content, its strings "
"won't show up in `locale/docs.pot`/ `locale/kmr/docs.po` for translators "
"until someone refreshes the catalog on purpose.  `po4a.cfg` reads six of the "
"seven component trees from `.translation-src/`, which only exists after "
"`make build` has cloned them, so run that at least once on a fresh checkout "
"first:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/translating.adoc:29
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"make build\n"
"po4a --keep 0 po4a.cfg\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/translating.adoc:33
msgid ""
"Review the diff (it should only ever add or reword entries, never delete "
"translated `msgstr`s for content that still exists) and commit the refreshed "
"catalog files."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/translating.adoc:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "Adding a new language"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/translating.adoc:40
msgid ""
"There's no generic multi-language machinery here on purpose -- each language "
"is wired up explicitly, by hand, following the same pattern as `kmr`. To add "
"locale `<code>` (an https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_639[ISO 639] code, "
"e.g. `kmr`, `es`, `fr`):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/translating.adoc:43
msgid ""
"**Extend `po4a.cfg`.** Add `<code>` to the `[po4a_langs]` line, and "
"duplicate every `[type: asciidoc]` line, replacing `kmr` with `<code>` in "
"each localized-file path."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/translating.adoc:48
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[po4a_langs] kmr <code>\n"
"[po4a_paths] locale/docs.pot $lang:locale/$lang/docs.po\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/translating.adoc:50
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[type: asciidoc] docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc "
"$lang:build/docs/$lang/home/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/translating.adoc:54
msgid ""
"(one `[type: asciidoc]` line per page + `nav.adoc`, across every component "
"-- see the existing file for the full list)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/translating.adoc:58
msgid ""
"**Generate the initial catalog.** From the repo root, with "
"https://po4a.org/[po4a] installed (and `make build` already run at least "
"once, so `.translation-src/` exists for `po4a.cfg` to read from):"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/translating.adoc:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "po4a --keep 0 po4a.cfg\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/translating.adoc:67
msgid ""
"Note there's no `--no-update` here: an initial catalog doesn't exist yet, "
"and `--no-update` prevents po4a from creating one from scratch, not just "
"from refreshing an existing one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/translating.adoc:70
msgid ""
"This creates `locale/<code>/docs.po` with every string present and blank "
"`msgstr`s. Commit it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/translating.adoc:74
msgid ""
"**Add a playbook for the new language.** Copy `antora-playbook-kmr.yml` to "
"`antora-playbook-<code>.yml`, and in the copy replace every "
"`build/docs/kmr/...` path with `build/docs/<code>/...`, and `output.dir` "
"with `./build/site/<code>`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/translating.adoc:78
msgid ""
"**Add the language to CI.** In `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`, duplicate the "
"\"Stage untranslated component trees\" and \"Build Kurmanji site\" steps for "
"`<code>` (pointing at `build/docs/<code>` and `antora-playbook-<code>.yml` "
"respectively)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/translating.adoc:82
msgid ""
"**Add the language to the switcher.** In "
"`supplemental-ui/partials/page-languages.hbs`, add one more `<a "
"class=\"language\">` entry (and extend the button-label conditional) for "
"`<code>`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/modules/ROOT/pages/translating.adoc:85
msgid ""
"Open a PR. Reviewers don't need to speak the language to merge it -- pages "
"render in English until a native speaker fills in `msgstr` entries in "
"`locale/<code>/docs.po` over time."
msgstr ""

