#, no-wrap
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:5
msgid ""
"Dengjen pulls its native dependencies (eSpeak-ng, Sonic, ...) in as git "
"submodules, so clone recursively:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/ZirekHQ/dengjen-tts.git\n"
"cd dengjen-tts\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:13
msgid "If you already cloned without `--recurse-submodules`, fetch them with:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "git submodule update --init --recursive\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:20
msgid "Then build the workspace, or just the CLI frontend:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:26
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"cargo build --release --workspace\n"
"# or just the CLI\n"
"cargo build --release -p dengjen-tts-cli\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:29
msgid ""
"The resulting binary is at `target/release/dengjen` (`dengjen.exe` on "
"Windows)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "Runtime data directory"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:35
msgid ""
"eSpeak-ng needs its `espeak-ng-data` directory at runtime. Dengjen looks for "
"it next to the running executable by default; if it lives elsewhere (or "
"you're running via `cargo run`), point to it with:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:39
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"export "
"DENGJEN_ESPEAKNG_DATA_DIRECTORY=/path/to/directory/containing/espeak-ng-data\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:42
msgid ""
"On Windows you also need `espeak-ng.dll` on your `PATH` — see "
"xref:testing.adoc[Testing] for the exact variable to set."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/testing.adoc:1
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/testing.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Testing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/testing.adoc:6
msgid ""
"Some packages, such as `espeak-phonemizer`, include tests. Running `cargo "
"test` from the root of the workspace will likely fail, because `cargo` does "
"not load `config` from sub packages when run from the workspace root."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/testing.adoc:11
msgid ""
"On Windows, `dengjen-espeak-rs-sys`'s build script copies the built "
"`espeak-ng.dll` into `target\\{profile}\\deps`, which is where `cargo test` "
"looks for it, so no `PATH` changes are normally needed. If a test binary "
"still can't find the DLL, add that directory to the library search path "
"before `cargo test`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/testing.adoc:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "set PATH=%PATH%;{repo_path}\\target\\debug\\deps\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/testing.adoc:18
msgid ""
"Replace `repo_path` with the absolute path to the repository, and `debug` "
"with `release` for a release build. Then `cd` to the package, and run `cargo "
"test` from there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Synthesizing speech"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:7
msgid ""
"Dengjen synthesizes speech from a https://github.com/rhasspy/piper[Piper] "
"voice. Download a voice's `.onnx` model and matching `.onnx.json` config "
"from the https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices[Piper voices] "
"repository and keep both files together, "
"e.g. `voices/en_US-lessac-medium.onnx` and "
"`voices/en_US-lessac-medium.onnx.json`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:15
msgid ""
"A voice doesn't have to come from the official Piper voices repository — any "
"VITS-family ONNX export using the same 3/4-input tensor convention (phoneme "
"ids, lengths, scales, optional speaker id) can be loaded by writing a "
"matching `.onnx.json` manifest with `\"model_type\": \"vits\"`. The minimal "
"required fields are `audio` (sample rate), `inference` "
"(`noise_scale`/`length_scale`/`noise_w`), and `phoneme_id_map` (the symbol "
"vocabulary); `phoneme_type` selects the phonemizer (`espeak` is the default "
"if omitted, and needs an `espeak.voice` entry — `text`, `hebrew`, and "
"`pinyin` don't)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:24
msgid ""
"A https://github.com/myshell-ai/MeloTTS[MeloTTS] voice — its own "
"VITS-derived ONNX export, with a `tones` tensor alongside phone ids — is "
"loaded with `\"model_type\": \"melotts\"`. The required fields are `audio` "
"(sample rate), `inference` (`noise_scale`/`length_scale`/`noise_scale_w`), "
"`phone_id_map` and `tone_id_map` (the phone and tone symbol vocabularies), "
"and `model_path`; `phonemizer` selects the phonemization backend and must be "
"one of `{\"type\": \"espeak\", \"voice\": \"<espeak-ng voice name>\"}` "
"(covers English, Spanish, French, Japanese, Korean) or `{\"type\": "
"\"pinyin\", \"model_dir\": \"<g2pW model directory>\"}` (Chinese, with real "
"tone extraction — requires building with the `pinyin` feature)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:25
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:89
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:55
#, no-wrap
msgid "CLI"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:28
msgid "Synthesize text from a file to a WAV file, using the `dengjen-cli` frontend:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:34
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"cargo run --release -p dengjen-tts-cli -- "
"voices/en_US-lessac-medium.onnx.json \\\n"
"    -f input.txt \\\n"
"    -o output.wav\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:37
msgid ""
"Or send a single request as JSON on stdin and capture the WAV bytes written "
"to stdout:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:41
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"echo '{\"text\": \"Hello world\"}' | cargo run --release -p dengjen-tts-cli "
"-- voices/en_US-lessac-medium.onnx.json > output.wav\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tts/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:44
msgid ""
"Run `dengjen --help` (or `cargo run --release -p dengjen-tts-cli -- --help`) "
"for the full list of options, including synthesis mode, speaker id, "
"rate/pitch/volume, and streaming chunk size."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/nav.adoc:5
msgid "xref:troubleshooting.adoc[Troubleshooting]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dengjen Neural Voices for NVDA"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:12
msgid ""
"*Project history.* Musharraf Omer (https://github.com/mush42[@mush42]) "
"created the original add-on and "
"https://nvda-addons.groups.io/g/nvda-addons/message/27636[announced on the "
"NVDA Add-ons list] that commercial contract conflicts prevent him from "
"continuing to maintain it. This project has continued it since, keeping the "
"add-on working on current NVDA releases, with compatibility updates "
"alongside bug fixes to the voice manager and the synthesizer driver. All "
"credit for the original work belongs to Musharraf Omer."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:15
msgid ""
"Renamed from Sonata Neural Voices in v4.0.0, at the original author's "
"request, as a condition of listing in the NVDA Add-on Store. Same add-on, "
"same maintainer, same GPL v2 licence."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:21
msgid ""
"This add-on adds neural text-to-speech voices to NVDA. It provides a "
"synthesizer driver for https://github.com/rhasspy/piper[Piper] voice models, "
"which run entirely on your own machine, plus a voice manager for downloading "
"and installing voices. An internet connection is needed to download voices, "
"but not to speak with them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:27
msgid ""
"Piper is a fast, local neural text-to-speech system that sounds great and is "
"optimized for low-end devices such as the Raspberry Pi. You can hear what "
"the voices sound like on the https://rhasspy.github.io/piper-samples/[Piper "
"voice samples] page. Speech is generated by "
"https://github.com/ZirekHQ/dengjen-tts[dengjen], a cross-platform Rust "
"engine for neural TTS models, originally based on "
"https://github.com/mush42/sonata[Sonata] by Musharraf Omer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:28
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:31
msgid "NVDA 2026.1 or later."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:36
msgid ""
"The https://aka.ms/vs/17/release/vc_redist.x64.exe[Microsoft Visual C++ "
"2015-2022 Redistributable (x64)].  The speech engine bundled with the add-on "
"is built with MSVC and cannot start without it. If it is missing, the add-on "
"shows a message pointing you to that download; install it and restart "
"NVDA. Most Windows machines already have it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:40
msgid ""
"Copyright(c) 2024, Musharraf Omer. Copyright(c) 2026, Ali Ustek and "
"contributors to this project.  Licensed under the GNU General Public License "
"Version 2 (GPL v2)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "Downloading the add-on"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:7
msgid ""
"You can find the add-on package under the assets section of the "
"https://github.com/ZirekHQ/dengjen-nvda/releases/latest[release page]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Adding voices"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:12
msgid ""
"The add-on is just a driver — it comes with no voices by default. You need "
"to download and install the voices you want from the voice manager."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:15
msgid ""
"Upon installing the add-on and restarting NVDA, the add-on will ask you to "
"download and install at least one voice, and it will give you the option to "
"open the voice manager."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:17
msgid "You can also open the voice manager from NVDA's main menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:21
msgid ""
"We recommend choosing the `low` or `medium` quality voices for your target "
"language(s), because they generally provide better responsiveness. For "
"additional responsiveness, you can choose to download the `fast` variant of "
"a voice at a cost of slightly lower speech quality."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:24
msgid ""
"You can also install voices from local archives. After obtaining the voice's "
"file, open the voice manager, in the installed tab, click the button labeled "
"`Install from local file`. Choose the voice file and wait for the voice to "
"install."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/troubleshooting.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/troubleshooting.adoc:7
msgid ""
"*Dengjen is missing from NVDA's synthesizer list, or fails to load.* The two "
"usual causes are the missing Visual C++ redistributable described in "
"xref:index.adoc[Requirements], and having no voices installed — the driver "
"deliberately refuses to load when it cannot find at least one voice. Open "
"the voice manager from NVDA's main menu, install a voice, then restart NVDA."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/troubleshooting.adoc:11
msgid ""
"*A voice I just downloaded is not offered in NVDA's voice list.* Restart "
"NVDA. A download refreshes the voice manager's own list, but NVDA may still "
"be holding the voice set it loaded at startup."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/troubleshooting.adoc:14
msgid ""
"*A preview or the voice list fails with a connection error.* Both are "
"fetched from the internet.  Check your connection, then use `Refresh voices "
"list` on the Download tab to retry."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/troubleshooting.adoc:17
msgid ""
"*\"You cannot remove the currently active voice!\"* Switch NVDA to a "
"different voice, or a different synthesizer, and then remove it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/troubleshooting.adoc:21
msgid ""
"*Speech is slow to start or stutters.* Prefer the `low` or `medium` quality "
"voices, and consider the `fast` variant of your voice. Higher quality models "
"need noticeably more processing per utterance."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/troubleshooting.adoc:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reporting issues"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/troubleshooting.adoc:25
msgid ""
"For anything else, NVDA's log usually says what went wrong: `NVDA menu` > "
"`Tools` > `View log`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/troubleshooting.adoc:28
msgid ""
"Please report bugs and feature requests on the "
"https://github.com/ZirekHQ/dengjen-nvda/issues[issue tracker], and include "
"the log along with your NVDA version and the voice you were using."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using the voice manager"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:5
msgid ""
"Open the voice manager from NVDA's main menu, under `Dengjen voice "
"manager...`. It has two tabs: `Download` and `Installed`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Download tab"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:10
msgid ""
"Choose a language from the `Language` dropdown to filter the `Available "
"voices` list, then select a voice to act on it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:14
msgid ""
"`Preview` plays a short sample of the selected voice so you can hear it "
"before downloading. The sample is streamed from the internet and nothing is "
"installed. While it is playing, the same button becomes `Stop preview`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:16
msgid ""
"`Speaker`, beside the preview button, is only enabled for voices trained "
"with more than one speaker. It selects which speaker the preview uses."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:19
msgid ""
"`Download standard variant` and `Download fast variant` fetch the "
"voice. Each button is disabled when that variant is already installed, and "
"the fast button is also disabled for voices that have no fast variant."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:21
msgid ""
"`Refresh voices list` fetches the catalogue again instead of reusing the "
"copy cached for this session."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "Installed tab"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:25
msgid ""
"The `Installed voices` list shows each installed voice with its variant, "
"quality and language."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:28
msgid ""
"`Voice model card...` displays the `MODEL_CARD` file shipped with the voice, "
"which records where its training data came from and how it is licensed. Not "
"every voice includes one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:31
msgid ""
"`Remove voice...` deletes the selected voice after asking you to confirm. It "
"stays disabled unless you have at least two voices installed, and it will "
"not remove the voice that is currently in use."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:32
msgid ""
"`Install from local file` installs a voice from a `.tar.gz` or `.tgz` "
"archive you already have."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:35
msgid ""
"`Import voices from Sonata` copies voices you downloaded with the older "
"Sonata Neural Voices add-on. It only appears while that add-on's voices are "
"still present and have not been imported yet. The originals are left in "
"place, so Sonata keeps working."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:39
msgid ""
"After installing from a local archive or removing a voice, the add-on "
"reloads the synthesizer for you, so the change applies immediately. After a "
"download the new voice shows up in the voice manager right away; if NVDA's "
"own voice list has not picked it up, restart NVDA."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "Voice settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:44
msgid ""
"With `Dengjen Neural Voices` selected as your synthesizer, the following "
"appear in NVDA's speech settings (`NVDA menu` > `Preferences` > `Settings` > "
"`Speech`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:46
msgid "`Voice` lists your installed voices as `name (language) - quality`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:49
msgid ""
"`Variant` switches between the `Standard` and `Fast` build of the current "
"voice. Only the variants you actually have installed are listed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:52
msgid ""
"`Speaker` applies to voices trained with several speakers; on a "
"single-speaker voice it has no effect. It is also available in the synth "
"settings ring."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:56
msgid ""
"`Rate`, `Volume` and `Pitch` behave as they do for any NVDA "
"synthesizer. With `Rate boost` turned off, the rate slider only covers the "
"lower part of the engine's speed range; turning it on spreads the slider "
"across the whole range, which allows much faster speech."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:57
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fine-tuning how a voice sounds"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:63
msgid ""
"`Length scale`, `Noise scale` and `Noise w` expose the Piper model's own "
"inference parameters.  All three work the same way: the slider runs from 0 "
"to 100, and 50 means the voice's trained default, so returning a slider to "
"50 undoes your changes to it. Of the three, only `Length scale` is offered "
"in the synth settings ring."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:68
msgid ""
"`Length scale` sets how long each speech sound is held. Higher values draw "
"speech out, lower values compress it. This is a separate mechanism from "
"`Rate` and the two combine, so it is usually easiest to set your speed with "
"`Rate` and only reach for this if a voice's natural pacing bothers you."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:70
msgid ""
"`Noise scale` sets how much variation the model puts into tone and "
"inflection. Higher values sound more expressive but less predictable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:72
msgid ""
"`Noise w` sets how much the duration of individual speech sounds varies, "
"which comes across as rhythm. Higher values sound less mechanical but can "
"blur articulation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:76
msgid ""
"Above 50, the sliders scale up to twice the voice's default for `Length "
"scale` and three times the default for `Noise scale` and `Noise w`. Because "
"50 always means \"this voice's default\", a given slider position keeps its "
"meaning when you switch to a different voice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:77
#, no-wrap
msgid "A note on voice quality"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:81
msgid ""
"The currently available voices are trained using freely available TTS "
"datasets, which are generally of low quality (mostly public domain audio "
"books or research-quality recordings)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:84
msgid ""
"Additionally, these datasets are not comprehensive, hence some voices may "
"exhibit incorrect or weird pronunciation. Both issues could be resolved by "
"using better datasets for training."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-nvda/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:86
msgid ""
"Luckily, the Piper developer and some developers from the blind and "
"vision-impaired community are working on training better voices."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/nav.adoc:4
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/nav.adoc:5
msgid "xref:building.adoc[Building]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "dengjen-piper-rs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:4
msgid "image:https://img.shields.io/crates/v/dengjen-piper-rs?logo=rust&color=F07B3C[Crates,link=https://crates.io/crates/dengjen-piper-rs/]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:6
msgid "Use https://github.com/OHF-Voice/piper1-gpl[Piper] TTS models in Rust."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:10
msgid "Compatibility with all Piper TTS models"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:11
msgid "Support for multiple languages"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:12
msgid ""
"High performance with a pure Rust API (eSpeak NG is vendored and built via "
