#. type: Title =
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/building.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Building a distributable binary"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/building.adoc:9
msgid ""
"`dengjen-espeak-rs-sys`'s build script compiles eSpeak NG's data files "
"(dictionaries, voices, phoneme tables) and, since it needs *some* directory "
"to build into, generates them inside "
"`target/<profile>/build/dengjen-espeak-rs-sys-<hash>/out/...` — an "
"ephemeral, cache-keyed path that disappears the moment `target/` is deleted "
"or the crate is rebuilt with a different hash.  Copying only the compiled "
"binary out of `target/` and discarding the rest (e.g.  `cargo build "
"--release` followed by `rm -rf target`) breaks it at runtime with:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/building.adoc:14
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Failed to initialize eSpeak-ng. Try setting "
"`PIPER_ESPEAKNG_DATA_DIRECTORY`\n"
"to the directory that contains the `espeak-ng-data` directory.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/building.adoc:19
msgid ""
"To make this easy, the build script also copies `espeak-ng-data` to "
"`target/<profile>/espeak-ng-data`, right next to the binary itself. At "
"runtime, `dengjen-espeak-rs` looks for `espeak-ng-data` (in this order) in:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/building.adoc:21
msgid "the directory named by the `PIPER_ESPEAKNG_DATA_DIRECTORY` env var,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/building.adoc:22
msgid "the current working directory,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/building.adoc:23
msgid "the directory containing the running executable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/building.adoc:26
msgid ""
"So for a plain `cargo build --release` / `cargo run --release`, it just "
"works — no env var needed, since (3) already finds "
"`target/release/espeak-ng-data`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/building.adoc:29
msgid ""
"To ship a binary elsewhere, copy both the binary and its `espeak-ng-data` "
"directory together and keep them side by side:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/building.adoc:36
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"cargo build --release\n"
"mkdir -p dist\n"
"cp target/release/<your-binary> dist/\n"
"cp -r target/release/espeak-ng-data dist/\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/building.adoc:41
msgid ""
"If your packaging can't keep them side by side (e.g. the data directory "
"belongs in a shared system location), set `PIPER_ESPEAKNG_DATA_DIRECTORY` at "
"runtime to the directory that *contains* `espeak-ng-data`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/building.adoc:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "Gotchas"
msgstr ""

