"make sure your Visual Studio is >= 17.11 (update through the Visual Studio "
"Installer)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/building.adoc:55
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-compiling for Linux arm64 (e.g. Raspberry Pi)"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/building.adoc:63
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sudo apt-get install crossbuild-essential-arm64 cmake pkg-config "
"libssl-dev\n"
"rustup target add aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu\n"
"CARGO_TARGET_AARCH64_UNKNOWN_LINUX_GNU_LINKER=aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc \\\n"
"  cargo build --release --target aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-piper-rs/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/building.adoc:70
msgid ""
"No `CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE`, sysroot variable, or separately-built `libasound` "
"is needed — the `cmake`/`cc` crates already recognize the standard "
"`aarch64-linux-gnu-*` cross-compiler naming convention that "
"`crossbuild-essential-arm64` installs, and eSpeak-ng's own CMake build skips "
"its tests and native-only intonation data when `CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING` is "
"set. `pkg-config`/ `libssl-dev` are only needed on the host, for the "
"`openssl-sys` build script (a build-time dependency of `ort`), not for the "
"arm64 target itself."
msgstr ""

