#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/speech.adoc:16
msgid ""
"`index()`, `clear()`, and `cancel()` are also available for tests that care "
"about ordering or interruption rather than just content."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/braille.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "nvda.braille"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/braille.adoc:4
msgid "The raw text sent to the braille display."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/braille.adoc:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"def test_my_addon_updates_braille(nvda, addon_under_test):\n"
"    before = nvda.braille.index()\n"
"    nvda.keys.press(\"NVDA+shift+b\")\n"
"    assert \"expected cell text\" in nvda.braille.since(before)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/braille.adoc:15
msgid ""
"Unlike the other namespace pages, this snippet is illustrative rather than "
"pulled from a real test — nothing in this kit's own suite currently drives a "
"braille display end to end."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/braille.adoc:18
msgid ""
"`index()`, `since()`, `all()`, and `last()` mirror "
"xref:guide/speech.adoc[`nvda.speech`]'s shape.  `wait_for` polls the same "
"way. `set_cell_count()` / `cell_count()` let a test simulate a display of a "
"given width, since braille output wraps differently depending on it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/keys.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "nvda.keys"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/keys.adoc:5
msgid ""
"Sending gestures through NVDA's own input pipeline — not simulated at the OS "
"level, so it exercises the same gesture-handling code your add-on's "
"`__gestures` map runs under."
