#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/keys.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"def test_a_gesture_reaches_nvda(nvda):\n"
"include::example$tests_e2e/test_smoke.py[tag=keys,indent=4]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/keys.adoc:14
msgid ""
"`sent()` returns every gesture NVDA has processed this session, in order — "
"useful for asserting that a gesture was actually delivered even when it "
"produces no speech or log line of its own."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/keys.adoc:15
msgid ""
"`type_text` and `press_all` cover typing a string and chording multiple "
"gestures."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/config.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "nvda.config"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/config.adoc:5
msgid ""
"Reading and writing NVDA's configuration, so a test can set up the exact "
"state your add-on's code path depends on."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/config.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"def test_config_round_trips_through_a_real_nvda(nvda):\n"
"include::example$tests_e2e/test_smoke.py[tag=config,indent=4]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/config.adoc:14
msgid ""
"`snapshot()` and `restore()` let a test change configuration for the "
"duration of one test and put it back afterwards, without needing to know "
"every key it touched:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/config.adoc:24
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"def test_something_under_a_changed_setting(nvda):\n"
"    snapshot = nvda.config.snapshot()\n"
"    try:\n"
"        nvda.config.set((\"speech\", \"symbolLevel\"), \"all\")\n"
"        ...\n"
"    finally:\n"
"        nvda.config.restore(snapshot)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/log.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "nvda.log"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/log.adoc:5
msgid ""
"Structured log records, and `assert_no_errors()` for the common case of \"my "
"add-on shouldn't have logged anything alarming.\""
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/log.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"def test_the_installed_addon_logs_at_startup(nvda, addon_under_test):\n"
"include::example$tests_e2e/test_demo_addon.py[tag=log,indent=4]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/log.adoc:15
msgid ""
"`wait_for` takes a regex and an index to search from — pass `since=0` (as "
"above) to search the whole session, or `since=nvda.log.index()` taken "
"earlier to ignore anything logged before that point."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/log.adoc:17
msgid ""
"`errors()` and `warnings()` filter by level; `assert_no_errors()` raises "
"with the offending records attached instead of returning a bare `False`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/addons.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "nvda.addons"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/addons.adoc:5
msgid ""
"Two-phase install, remove, and state — install and remove only take effect "
"after NVDA restarts, matching how NVDA itself behaves outside tests."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/addons.adoc:36
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|`AddonState` |Meaning\n"
"\n"
"|`NOT_INSTALLED`\n"
"|no trace of the add-on\n"
"\n"
"|`PENDING_INSTALL`\n"
"|installed, waiting for the restart that enables it\n"
"\n"
"|`ENABLED`\n"
"|installed and running\n"
"\n"
"|`DISABLED`\n"
"|installed but turned off\n"
"\n"
"|`PENDING_REMOVE`\n"
"|marked for removal, waiting for the restart that completes it\n"
"\n"
"|`INCOMPATIBLE`\n"
"|installed, but NVDA refuses to enable it\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/nvda-addon-testkit/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/guide/addons.adoc:40
msgid ""
"Most tests don't need this directly — the "
"xref:guide/fixtures.adoc[`addon_under_test` fixture] already does the "
"install-and-restart dance for you. Reach for `nvda.addons` yourself only "
"when a test is about the install/remove lifecycle itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "dengjen-tashkeel"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:5
msgid ""
"Arabic-text diacritic (tashkeel) restoration using an ONNX neural model, "
"trained mainly on MSA data from https://github.com/mush42/hareef[Hareef]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:7
msgid ""
"Available as a Rust crate, a C ABI, a Python package, a Java library, and a "
"standalone CLI."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Non-scope"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:11
msgid "Diacritization only — not a general-purpose Arabic NLP toolkit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "Known limitation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:20
msgid ""
"Accuracy is bounded by the underlying Hareef model: it can mis-diacritize "
"proper nouns and other words whose correct case ending depends on context it "
"wasn't trained to resolve. For example, given `عن أمير المؤمنين أبي حفص عمر "
"بن الخطاب`, the name `حفص` comes out as `حِفَصِ` (\"hifsi\")  instead of the "
"grammatically correct `حَفْصٍ` (\"hafsin\"). See "
"https://github.com/ZirekHQ/dengjen-tashkeel/issues/28[issue #28] for the "
"full discrepancy. This is a model-accuracy limitation, not a bug in this "
"library's code."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:24
msgid "Created by https://github.com/mush42[mush42] (Musharraf Omer)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/index.adoc:27
msgid "Dual-licensed under MIT or Apache-2.0, at your option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:3
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rust"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "cargo add dengjen-tashkeel\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:12
msgid ""
"The default features (`ort-static`, `rayon`) statically link a bundled ONNX "
"Runtime, so this works with no extra setup."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:13
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:19
#, no-wrap
msgid "Python"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "pip install dengjen-tashkeel-py\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:25
msgid ""
"Published to PyPI as `dengjen-tashkeel-py` by the `python-publish.yml` CI "
"workflow whenever a version tag is pushed — availability at any given moment "
"depends on whether a tag has been pushed since this was set up, so if the "
"install fails, build the wheel yourself instead (see "
"xref:building.adoc[Building]). The wheel depends on `onnxruntime` (installed "
"automatically by `pip`); don't have `onnxruntime-gpu` installed alongside it "
"— they share the same import name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:26
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "C"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:32
msgid ""
"Download the prebuilt `dengjen-tashkeel-capi-<target>` archive for your "
"platform from https://github.com/ZirekHQ/dengjen-tashkeel/releases[GitHub "
"Releases]. Each archive bundles the built shared library "
"(`.so`/`.dylib`/`.dll`) together with `dengjen_tashkeel.h` — link against "
"the library and include the header, no need to build from source."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:37
msgid ""
"The library and header are also available through a self-hosted "
"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/vcpkg/consuming/git-registries[vcpkg "
"custom registry] — this repository itself, referenced directly by git, no "
"separate server needed. Add it to your project's `vcpkg-configuration.json`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:54
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"default-registry\": {\n"
"    \"kind\": \"builtin\",\n"
"    \"baseline\": \"<current vcpkg builtin-registry baseline>\"\n"
"  },\n"
"  \"registries\": [\n"
"    {\n"
"      \"kind\": \"git\",\n"
"      \"repository\": \"https://github.com/ZirekHQ/dengjen-tashkeel\",\n"
"      \"baseline\": \"<commit-sha of the dengjen-tashkeel commit to "
"pin>\",\n"
"      \"packages\": [\"dengjen-tashkeel-capi\"]\n"
"    }\n"
"  ]\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:57
msgid ""
"then add `dengjen-tashkeel-capi` to your `vcpkg.json` dependencies and run "
"`vcpkg install`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:62
msgid ""
"https://github.com/conan-io/conan-center-index[ConanCenter] requires recipes "
"to build from source, which this project's C API can't do without a Rust "
"toolchain in Conan's build environment, so this isn't published "
"there. Instead, clone this repository and export the recipe into your local "
"Conan cache:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "conan create packaging/conan --version=1.5.3\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:70
msgid ""
"then add `dengjen-tashkeel-capi/1.5.3` to your "
"`conanfile.txt`/`conanfile.py` `requires`. See `packaging/README.md` in the "
"repository for how both are maintained."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:71
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:38
#, no-wrap
msgid "Java"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:77
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"implementation(\"io.github.zirekhq:dengjen-tashkeel:1.5.3\")\n"
"runtimeOnly(\"io.github.zirekhq:dengjen-tashkeel:1.5.3:linux-x86_64\")\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:88
msgid ""
"Published to Maven Central by the `java-publish.yml` CI workflow whenever a "
"version tag is pushed. The binding uses the JDK Foreign Function & Memory "
"API (`java.lang.foreign`), not JNA, to load the native "
"`dengjen_tashkeel_capi` shared library. The native library ships as "
"per-platform classifier jars — `linux-x86_64`, `windows-x64`, and "
"`macos-aarch64` — so add a `runtimeOnly` dependency on the one matching your "
"platform alongside the main dependency; it's picked up automatically at "
"runtime. To use a library you built or placed yourself instead, set "
"`-Ddengjen.tashkeel.native.library.path=/path/to/library` (a file path, not "
"a directory — `java.library.path` is not consulted). Either way, add "
"`--enable-native-access=ALL-UNNAMED` to your own JVM invocation to avoid a "
"native-access warning."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:92
msgid "Either build from source (see xref:building.adoc[Building]) or:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/installation.adoc:96
#, no-wrap
msgid "cargo install dengjen-tashkeel-cli\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quick start"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "use dengjen_tashkeel::{create_inference_engine, do_tashkeel};\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:12
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"// None = use the bundled model.\n"
"let engine = create_inference_engine(None)?;\n"
"let diacritized = do_tashkeel(&engine, \"بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم\", None, "
"false)?;\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:18
msgid ""
"`do_tashkeel`'s third argument is an optional taskeen threshold (see below) "
"and the fourth is `preprocessed` — pass `true` only if `text` is already "
"sentence-segmented, otherwise the library segments it for you. Input is "
"capped at `CHAR_LIMIT` (12,000 characters); longer input returns "
"`Err(DengjenTashkeelError::InputTooLong(_))`."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "from dengjen_tashkeel_py import tashkeel\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:26
#, no-wrap
msgid "tashkeel(\"بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم\")\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:31
msgid ""
"The Rust side logs via the `log` facade but installs no backend; if you want "
"its diagnostics (e.g. a redundant-init warning) surfaced through Python's "
"own `logging` module, install https://github.com/vorner/pyo3-log[pyo3-log] "
"in your embedding process."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:37
msgid ""
"The API is a single entry point for diacritizing a UTF-8 encoded string — "
"see `crates/capi/ffi_usage_example.py` in the repository for sample usage "
"against the compiled library via `ctypes`."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:44
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"import io.github.zirekhq.dengjen.tashkeel.Tashkeel;\n"
"import java.util.Optional;\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:47
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Tashkeel tashkeel = Tashkeel.loadDefault();\n"
"String diacritized = tashkeel.diacritize(\"بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم\", "
"Optional.empty(), false);\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:54
msgid ""
"`diacritize`'s second argument is an optional taskeen threshold (see below) "
"and the third is `preprocessed` — pass `true` only if the text is already "
"sentence-segmented, otherwise the library segments it for you. Errors "
"surface as a checked `TashkeelException`, whose `reason()` is an "
"exhaustively switchable sealed type mirroring the `ErrorCode` values in "
"`dengjen_tashkeel.h`."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:61
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"echo \"بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم\" > input.txt\n"
"dengjen-tashkeel -f input.txt\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "Usage: dengjen-tashkeel [OPTIONS]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:76
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Options:\n"
"  -f, --input-file <INPUT_FILE>    Input file (default `stdin`)\n"
"  -o, --output-file <OUTPUT_FILE>  Output file (default `stdout`)\n"
"  -i, --interactive                Use interactive mode (useful for "
"testing)\n"
"  -t, --taskeen                    Use sukoon for case-ending diacritic if "
"the model is uncertain\n"
"  -p, --prob <PROB>                Taskeen threshold probability [default: "
"0.95]\n"
"  -x, --onnx <ONNX_MODEL>          ONNX model (default: use bundled model if "
"available)\n"
"  -h, --help                       Print help\n"
"  -V, --version                    Print version\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:79
msgid ""
"With neither `--input-file` nor `--output-file`, the CLI runs in interactive "
"mode by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "The taskeen option"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/dengjen-tashkeel/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/usage.adoc:83
msgid ""
"When enabled (`taskeen_threshold` in Rust/Python, `--taskeen`/`--prob` in "
"the CLI), the model substitutes a sukoon for a case-ending diacritic it "
"isn't confident about, instead of guessing."
msgstr ""

