#. type: Title =
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/getting_started.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/getting_started.adoc:4
msgid ""
"This plugin will register itself with the Pact framework for the "
"`avro/binary`,`application/avro`, `application/*+avro` and `avro/bytes` "
"content types."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/getting_started.adoc:7
msgid ""
"Using this plugin, you can write Pact tests that verify a single message "
"(i.e. a message provider sends a message to a consumer)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/getting_started.adoc:9
msgid ""
"Tests are supported by using the V4 asynchronous message Pact format, and "
"the service method calls use the V4 synchronous message Pact format."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/getting_started.adoc:13
msgid ""
"The executable binaries and plugin manifest file for the plugin can be "
"downloaded from the project link:../releases[releases page]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/getting_started.adoc:16
msgid ""
"Plugin installation requires the plugin executable binary as well as the "
"plugin manifest file to be unpacked/copied into a Pact plugin directory. By "
"default, this will be `.pact/plugins/avro-<version>` in the home directory "
"(i.e.  `$HOME/.pact/plugins/avro-{version}` for version {version})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/getting_started.adoc:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "Automated"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/getting_started.adoc:20
msgid ""
"The "
"https://github.com/pact-foundation/pact-plugins/tree/main/cli[pact-plugin-cli] "
"can be used to install the Avro plugin. See the "
"https://github.com/pact-foundation/pact-plugins/tree/main/cli#installing[CLI "
"installation] on how to install it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/getting_started.adoc:22
msgid "To install the latest version, run"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/getting_started.adoc:26
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"pact-plugin-cli -y install "
"https://github.com/austek/pact-avro-plugin/releases/latest\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/getting_started.adoc:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "Manual"
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/getting_started.adoc:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run install-plugin.sh:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/getting_started.adoc:34
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"wget -O - "
"https://github.com/austek/pact-avro-plugin/releases/latest/download/install-plugin.sh "
"| bash\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/getting_started.adoc:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "INFORMATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/getting_started.adoc:36
msgid ""
"The default plugin directory (`$HOME/.pact/plugins`) can be changed by "
"setting the `PACT_PLUGIN_DIR` environment variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/testing.adoc:4
msgid ""
"For an overview how asynchronous messages work with Pact, see "
"https://docs.pact.io/getting_started/how_pact_works/#non-http-testing-message-pact[Non-HTTP "
"testing (Message Pact)]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/testing.adoc:7
msgid ""
"In this scenario, a message provider writes a Protocol Buffer message to "
"some one-way transport mechanism, like a message queue, and a consumer then "
"reads it. With this style of testing, the transport mechanism is abstracted "
"away."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/testing.adoc:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consumer"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/testing.adoc:11
msgid ""
"The message consumer test is written using the Pact Message test DSL. The "
"test DSL defines the expected message format, and then the consumer is "
"tested with an example message generated by the test framework."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/testing.adoc:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Avro test configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/testing.adoc:17
msgid ""
"The consumer tests need to get the plugin loaded and configure the expected "
"messages to use in the test. This is done using the `usingPlugin` (or "
"`using_plugin`, depending on the language implementation) followed by the "
"content for the test in some type of map form."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/testing.adoc:20
msgid ""
"For each field of the message that we want in the contract, we define an "
"entry with the field name as the key and a matching definition as the "
"value. For documentation on the matching definition format, see "
"https://github.com/pact-foundation/pact-plugins/blob/main/docs/matching-rule-definition-expressions.md[Matching "
"Rule definition expressions]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: .translation-src/pact-avro-plugin/docs/modules/ROOT/pages/testing.adoc:22
msgid ""
"For example, for a JVM test (taken from "
"https://developers.google.com/protocol-buffers/docs/javatutorial[Protocol "
"Buffer Java examples]) we would use the PactBuilder class:"
msgstr ""

